From 8477545cb99bb64829f74a51c2925591e502c127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jackwang0009 <93422958+jackwang0009@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:47:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] [upstream-candidate] Preserve text clip modes (Tr 4-7) across
 content rewrite
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CPDF_PageContentGenerator wrote each text object on its own and closed the
enclosing `q` immediately, so a text clip (Tr 4-7) never stayed open across
the objects it was meant to clip. Keep clip-mode texts as an open group:
match consecutive Tr 4-7 texts against the clip text list of the next
active object, write one `q` plus the shared path clip, emit one BT...ET
per original group (glyph union within a group, intersection across
groups, as the renderer does), and only close the `q` once later objects
no longer need that clip.

Helpers: WriteClipPath / WriteGraphicsState / WriteTextContent /
WriteTextClipGroup / CanWriteText, plus TextClipSignature matching so
clip-path clones can be identified by value.

Tests: CPDFPageContentGeneratorTest.ProcessTextClipGroup.

Verification (ops_diff.py): synthetic colour diffs stay 0; text-clip-modes
keeps clip_text 6→6 (remaining pixel diff is shading_lost, V03 item 6);
no-diff pages 54/67 synthetic, 384/388 public.
